          "content": "## Unit orientation\n\nThis unit asks what can and cannot be concluded from observations in the running case. Begin by listing state variables and the time basis, identifying which quantities have been measured and which are assumptions. The engineering task is to distinguish evidence of transport, transformation, dilution and removal, and to prevent an untested model from becoming a safety claim. Compare at least two approaches with the same functional requirements, and include one sensitivity or uncertainty test in the written submission."
