          "heading": "Check 05: Particle-settling threshold",
          "content": "## Check 05: Particle-settling threshold\n\nA basin with 5,000 m\u00b3/day flow and 250 m\u00b2 plan area has 20 m/day surface overflow velocity. Ideal particles with 25 m/day settling velocity satisfy the basic capture threshold; particles at 10 m/day do not. The concept is geometric rather than a guarantee of actual removal because a real suspension contains a distribution of velocities. Determine how much extra area would be needed for the slower particle to meet the ideal threshold and identify why hydraulic bypass or turbulence can still reduce performance. Record which assumptions a settling-column test can investigate."
