          "heading": "Check 07: Integrated disinfection exposure",
          "content": "## Check 07: Integrated disinfection exposure\n\nFor C\u2080=1.5 mg/L, k=0.025 min\u207b\u00b9, and contact 40 min, final modelled residual is about 0.552 mg/L. The integral of residual over that period is 1.5(1\u2212e\u207b\u00b9)/0.025\u224837.93 mg\u00b7min/L. The common calculation of initial residual times nominal contact time would give 60 mg\u00b7min/L and overstate the decaying-residual area. Neither value authorizes pathogen log removal without validated microbial kinetics, temperature and hydraulic contact time. Explain why a tank with long short-circuiting tails may invalidate a mean-time estimate."
