          "content": "## Check 11: Dispersion and limitations of a plume peak\n\nThe simplified centreline Gaussian model combines source emission rate, mean wind speed and width parameters that increase with distance. Holding everything else fixed, doubling source rate doubles predicted concentration; doubling wind speed halves it in this approximation. Real plume rise and atmospheric stability can alter both relationships. Demonstrate in the simulation that the near-field curve is not necessarily maximal close to the stack because effective release height delays ground interaction. Compare with a regulatory dispersion model checklist."
