          "heading": "Check 12: Testing particle removal with actual flow",
          "content": "## Check 12: Testing particle removal with actual flow\n\nAn inlet of 100 mg/m\u00b3 at 9,000 m\u00b3/h corresponds to 0.9 kg/h particles. At 96% mass removal, captured mass is 0.864 kg/h and outlet mass is 0.036 kg/h, assuming unchanged standardized gas flow. If outlet flow is measured at a different temperature or pressure basis, direct concentration subtraction is not legitimate. Specify normalized sampling, control uptime, bypass status and particle-size sensitivity. Explain how collected dust needs an additional waste or reuse assessment."
