          "content": "## Check 14: First-order gas timing and capture schedule\n\nFor 100,000 t of deposited waste, gas potential 120 m\u00b3/t and k=0.05 year\u207b\u00b9, year-zero generation is 600,000 m\u00b3/year, declining to about 363,918 m\u00b3/year after ten years. If gas collection begins only after several years, early generated gas may not be captured. The integrated modelled potential is 12 million m\u00b3 over an infinite horizon, independent of k, but the fraction collected depends on operating schedule and actual site conditions. Distinguish gross generation from methane emissions measured at the surface."
