          "heading": "Check 16: Electricity boundary and an uncertain grid",
          "content": "## Check 16: Electricity boundary and an uncertain grid\n\nAt 15,000 m\u00b3/day and 0.4 kWh/m\u00b3 the plant uses 6,000 kWh/day. An illustrative electricity factor 0.5 kg CO\u2082e/kWh gives 3,000 kg CO\u2082e/day; a factor 0.2 gives 1,200 kg CO\u2082e/day without changing treatment. Emission-factor choice can dominate comparisons. Report the spatial and temporal basis of the factor and avoid double counting any solar electricity. Direct methane, nitrous oxide, chemical manufacture and residual transport remain outside this model.\n\n# Evidence-driven case bank: eight additional field scenarios\n\nThese exercises ask the student to identify missing measurements, trace mass or energy through a real-world system boundary and evaluate competing explanations. Numerical values are teaching examples; not independently measured field datasets."
