          "secNumber": "8.48",
          "heading": "Case 1: environmental systems field decision",
          "content": "## Case 1: environmental systems field decision\n\nA coastal drainage basin contains a tidal gate and intermittently operating pumps. A plume appearing upstream of the discharge point does not necessarily violate mass balance because flow direction reverses during certain tides. Construct an observation table with tide phase, pump state, tracer concentration and salinity. Estimate net mass transfer by integrating signed discharge rather than using the largest measured flow. If rainfall causes pump cycling, an hourly mean may conceal the event. Compare a continuous sensor with a three-sample grab campaign. Conclude with a data-quality objective for declaring whether the industrial discharge or saline intrusion dominates the observed concentration change."
