          "content": "## Case 2: environmental systems field decision\n\nA river laboratory reports total nitrogen as 12 mg/L at the upstream site, while another reports nitrate at 15 mg/L as NO\u2083\u207b downstream. The numbers cannot be compared directly as if they represented the same nitrogen quantity. Convert nitrate-ion concentration to nitrate as nitrogen using molecular weights, then identify the remaining nitrogen species. Establish whether total nitrogen should include dissolved and particulate material. Propose a method intercomparison and chain-of-custody test before interpreting a trend. Explain why adding unverified values from incompatible species can violate constituent accounting, even if each laboratory result was analytically correct."
