          "content": "## Case 7: environmental systems field decision\n\nAn environmental assessment for a new industrial estate models traffic noise but not runoff contaminated by construction soil or sediment. Define the drainage area, receiving water, construction periods and possible mitigation controls. Ask for baseline suspended-solids data at storm and nonstorm flows and clarify how flood-driven sediment transport could impact a sensitive wetland. Set up measurable performance indicators, such as protected outfall observations and validated turbidity/solids sampling. Explain how an incomplete impact register creates regulatory and financial risk, and how compensating for unavoidable impacts differs from preventing avoidable ones."
